J313 (MacBook Air M1) speakers: end the woofer path with a true-peak limiter.

The woofer_lim compressor lets transients through, so on bass-heavy material
the graph sends samples up to +7 dBFS to the amps, which hard-clip them before
speakersafetyd can act (crackle on bass hits).  An LSP limiter_stereo at
-1 dBFS (th 0.891), 5 ms lookahead, no level regulation or boost, only lowers
those peaks.

Taken from Aurora Silicon's asahi-audio fork, commit
b30c50aa0e461eaf75e7363d8cba644730d80d82 by Ryan Murray
(https://github.com/aurora-silicon/asahi-audio), the J313 hunk only.
Licence: MIT, same as asahi-audio (Copyright (c) 2022 The Asahi Linux
Contributors).

